#. type: Title =
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-client-configuration.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "MCP Client Configuration"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-client-configuration.adoc:2
msgid ""
"This chapter provides example stdio and HTTP client configurations and "
"explains how to verify the integration."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-client-configuration.adoc:3
msgid ""
"MCP configuration formats differ across various clients.  Use the examples "
"in this chapter as a template and consult the client documentation for the "
"exact property names and configuration file location."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-client-configuration.adoc:4
#, no-wrap
msgid "Configure a stdio client"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-client-configuration.adoc:5
msgid ""
"The following generic configuration starts a container for each MCP client "
"session:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-client-configuration.adoc:6
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"mcpServers\": {\n"
"    \"mcp-server-uyuni\": {\n"
"      \"command\": \"podman\",\n"
"      \"args\": [\n"
"        \"run\",\n"
"        \"-i\",\n"
"        \"--rm\",\n"
"        \"--env-file\",\n"
"        \"/absolute/path/to/mcp.env\",\n"
"        \"registry.suse.com/suse/agentic/mcp/multi-linux-manager:<version>\"\n"
"      ]\n"
"    }\n"
"  }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-client-configuration.adoc:7
msgid ""
"The `-i` option is required because MCP uses the container's standard input "
"and output.  Use an absolute path to the environment file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-client-configuration.adoc:8
#, no-wrap
msgid "Configure an HTTP client"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-client-configuration.adoc:9
msgid ""
"After deploying the standalone server, configure the client with its "
"streamable HTTP endpoint:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-client-configuration.adoc:10
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"mcpServers\": {\n"
"    \"mcp-server-uyuni\": {\n"
"      \"url\": \"https://mcp.example.com/mcp\",\n"
"      \"type\": \"http\"\n"
"    }\n"
"  }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-client-configuration.adoc:11
msgid ""
"The client must be able to complete OAuth authorization against the issuer "
"configured with `UYUNI_AUTH_SERVER`.  The exact transport name in a client "
"configuration can be `http` or `streamable-http`, depending on the client."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-client-configuration.adoc:12
#, no-wrap
msgid "Verify the integration"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-client-configuration.adoc:13
msgid ""
"Restart the MCP client after changing its configuration.  Then make low-"
"risk, read-only requests, for example:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-client-configuration.adoc:14
msgid "\"List the first five active systems.\""
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-client-configuration.adoc:15
msgid "\"Find systems with `web` in the hostname.\""
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-client-configuration.adoc:16
msgid "\"List the first ten systems that need a reboot.\""
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-client-configuration.adoc:17
msgid ""
"Confirm that the returned system names and IDs are aligned with the "
"{productname} {webui}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-client-configuration.adoc:18
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use tools efficiently"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-client-configuration.adoc:19
msgid ""
"MCP tool output consumes AI context.  When explicitly selecting tools, "
"directing an assistant to use a particular tool, or implementing an agent "
"workflow, apply these practices:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-client-configuration.adoc:20
msgid "Start with `summarize_system_updates` or `summarize_fleet_updates`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-client-configuration.adoc:21
msgid "Use pagination parameters and follow `meta.next_offset`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-client-configuration.adoc:22
msgid "Set `include_cves` or `include_updates` only when details are required."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-client-configuration.adoc:23
msgid ""
"Use `find_systems_by_name` before a tool call when a hostname is ambiguous."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-client-configuration.adoc:24
msgid ""
"Ask the assistant to show the target system ID, action ID, or erratum ID "
"before a state-changing call."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-concepts.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Concepts and Architecture"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-concepts.adoc:2
msgid ""
"This chapter introduces the components, request flow, deployment models, and "
"capabilities of the {productname} MCP Server."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-concepts.adoc:3
msgid ""
"The Model Context Protocol (MCP) is an open protocol that allows an AI "
"application to discover and call tools exposed by an external server.  The "
"{productname} MCP Server implements MCP tools that translate structured tool "
"calls into {productname} HTTP API requests."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-concepts.adoc:4
msgid ""
"The MCP Server integrates with the existing {productname} authorization "
"model.  The authenticated account determines which content is visible and "
"which operations are permitted."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-concepts.adoc:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "Components"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-concepts.adoc:6
msgid "An MCP integration contains the following components:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-concepts.adoc:7
#, no-wrap
msgid "MCP host"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-concepts.adoc:8
msgid "The AI application in which the user works."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-concepts.adoc:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "MCP client"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-concepts.adoc:10
msgid ""
"The protocol client maintained by the host.  It discovers tools, sends tool "
"calls, displays progress and results, and can request user approval."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-concepts.adoc:11
msgid ""
"{productname} MCP Server:: The process that exposes tools over stdio or "
"streamable HTTP and calls the {productname} API."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-concepts.adoc:12
msgid ""
"{productname} Server:: The managed infrastructure service and authorization "
"boundary."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-concepts.adoc:13
#, no-wrap
msgid "Identity provider"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-concepts.adoc:14
msgid ""
"An optional OAuth 2.0/OpenID Connect provider used for a shared HTTP "
"deployment."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-concepts.adoc:15
#, no-wrap
msgid "Request flow"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-concepts.adoc:16
msgid "For a read-only request, the flow is:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-concepts.adoc:17
msgid ""
"The user asks the AI assistant to retrieve information from {productname}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-concepts.adoc:18
msgid "The AI assistant selects an MCP tool and supplies structured arguments."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-concepts.adoc:19
msgid "The MCP client sends the tool call to the MCP Server."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-concepts.adoc:20
msgid ""
"The MCP Server authenticates to {productname}, calls the corresponding API, "
"and normalizes the response."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-concepts.adoc:21
msgid "The MCP client returns the structured result to the AI assistant."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-concepts.adoc:22
msgid ""
"State-changing tools add an approval step when the MCP client supports MCP "
"elicitation.  For more information, see xref:mcp-server-security.adoc#write-"
"tool-controls[Write tool controls]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-concepts.adoc:23
#, no-wrap
msgid "Deployment models"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-concepts.adoc:24
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"|Model\n"
"|Use case\n"
"|Characteristics\n"
"\n"
"|Client-managed stdio\n"
"|One user or one local AI application\n"
"|The MCP client starts one server process. Communication remains on stdin and stdout. {productname} credentials are normally supplied to that process.\n"
"\n"
"|Standalone HTTP\n"
"|A persistent service shared by multiple users or clients\n"
"|Clients connect to `/mcp` over streamable HTTP. OAuth is strongly recommended. Production deployments should expose the endpoint only over TLS.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-concepts.adoc:25
msgid ""
"Use client-managed stdio unless the MCP Server must be shared or centrally "
"operated.  The smaller network surface and process lifetime make stdio "
"easier to secure."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-concepts.adoc:26
#, no-wrap
msgid "Capabilities and limitations"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-concepts.adoc:27
msgid ""
"The server exposes MCP tools for systems, updates, CVEs, actions, activation "
"keys, and system groups.  Write tools are disabled by default.  The server "
"does not expose MCP resources or prompts."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-concepts.adoc:28
msgid ""
"Tool results can be paginated to reduce context usage.  For fleet-wide "
"questions, use summary tools first and request detailed update or CVE data "
"only when required."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-concepts.adoc:29
msgid ""
"An AI-generated explanation is not an authoritative record of system state.  "
"Review the structured tool result and confirm important changes in the "
"{productname} {webui}, especially after scheduling updates, rebooting, "
"bootstrapping, or removing systems."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-configuration.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Server Configuration"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-configuration.adoc:2
msgid ""
"This chapter describes the environment variables for configuring the "
"{productname} connection, transport, tools, logging, and system bootstrap."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-configuration.adoc:3
#, no-wrap
msgid "{productname} connection"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-configuration.adoc:4
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"|Variable\n"
"|Required\n"
"|Default\n"
"|Description\n"
"\n"
"|`UYUNI_SERVER`\n"
"|Yes\n"
"|-\n"
"|Base URL of the {productname} Server. If the scheme is omitted, `https` is used. A path, query, or fragment is not allowed.\n"
"\n"
"|`UYUNI_USER`\n"
"|For basic auth\n"
"|-\n"
"|{productname} user name. Use with `UYUNI_PASS` when `UYUNI_AUTH_SERVER` is not set.\n"
"\n"
"|`UYUNI_PASS`\n"
"|For basic auth\n"
"|-\n"
"|Password for `UYUNI_USER`.\n"
"\n"
"|`UYUNI_MCP_SSL_VERIFY`\n"
"|No\n"
"|`true`\n"
"|Verifies the TLS certificate presented by the {productname} Server. Values `false`, `0`, and `no` disable verification.\n"
"\n"
"|`UYUNI_MCP_TIMEOUT`\n"
"|No\n"
"|`30`\n"
"|HTTP request timeout in seconds. The connection timeout remains 10 seconds.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-configuration.adoc:5
msgid ""
"Do not disable certificate verification in production.  Install the issuing "
"CA certificate in the container or host trust store instead."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-configuration.adoc:6
#, no-wrap
msgid "Transport and service"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-configuration.adoc:7
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"|Variable\n"
"|Required\n"
"|Default\n"
"|Description\n"
"\n"
"|`UYUNI_MCP_TRANSPORT`\n"
"|No\n"
"|`stdio`\n"
"|Transport mode. Valid values are `stdio` and `http`.\n"
"\n"
"|`UYUNI_MCP_HOST`\n"
"|HTTP only\n"
"|`127.0.0.1`\n"
"|Address on which the HTTP server listens.\n"
"\n"
"|`UYUNI_MCP_PORT`\n"
"|HTTP only\n"
"|`8000`\n"
"|Port on which the HTTP server listens.\n"
"\n"
"|`UYUNI_MCP_PUBLIC_URL`\n"
"|OAuth HTTP deployment\n"
"|Derived from host and port\n"
"|External base URL advertised to OAuth-capable clients. Set the client-facing URL, without `/mcp`.\n"
"\n"
"|`UYUNI_AUTH_SERVER`\n"
"|Recommended for HTTP\n"
"|-\n"
"|OpenID Connect issuer URL. A path is allowed. When omitted, the MCP HTTP endpoint does not authenticate clients.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-configuration.adoc:8
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tools and logging"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-configuration.adoc:9
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"|Variable\n"
"|Required\n"
"|Default\n"
"|Description\n"
"\n"
"|`UYUNI_MCP_WRITE_TOOLS_ENABLED`\n"
"|No\n"
"|`false`\n"
"|Registers tools that modify {productname}. Values `true`, `1`, and `yes` enable them.\n"
"\n"
"|`UYUNI_MCP_LOG_FILE_PATH`\n"
"|No\n"
"|Console\n"
"|Path to the server log file.\n"
"\n"
"|`UYUNI_MCP_LOG_LEVEL`\n"
"|No\n"
"|`INFO`\n"
"|Logging level, for example `DEBUG`, `INFO`, `WARNING`, `ERROR`, or `CRITICAL`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-configuration.adoc:10
msgid ""
"Changing `UYUNI_MCP_WRITE_TOOLS_ENABLED` requires a process restart because "
"the server registers tools during startup."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-configuration.adoc:11
#, no-wrap
msgid "System bootstrap"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-configuration.adoc:12
msgid "The `add_system` tool requires these additional variables:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-configuration.adoc:13
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"|Variable\n"
"|Required\n"
"|Description\n"
"\n"
"|`UYUNI_SSH_PRIV_KEY`\n"
"|For `add_system`\n"
"|Private SSH key used to bootstrap the target. Store the key as one line with each newline represented by the literal `\\n` sequence.\n"
"\n"
"|`UYUNI_SSH_PRIV_KEY_PASS`\n"
"|No\n"
"|Passphrase for the private SSH key.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-configuration.adoc:14
msgid ""
"Do not place the key directly in an MCP client configuration that is "
"synchronized or shared.  Prefer a protected environment file or a secrets-"
"management system."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-configuration.adoc:15
#, no-wrap
msgid "Example read-only configuration"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-configuration.adoc:16
msgid ""
"The following example uses basic authentication with `UYUNI_USER` and "
"`UYUNI_PASS`."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-configuration.adoc:17
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"UYUNI_SERVER=https://server.example.com\n"
"UYUNI_USER=mcp-reader\n"
"UYUNI_PASS=replace-me\n"
"UYUNI_MCP_SSL_VERIFY=true\n"
"UYUNI_MCP_TIMEOUT=30\n"
"UYUNI_MCP_TRANSPORT=stdio\n"
"UYUNI_MCP_WRITE_TOOLS_ENABLED=false\n"
"UYUNI_MCP_LOG_LEVEL=INFO\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-installation.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Installation and Deployment"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-installation.adoc:2
msgid ""
"This chapter describes the requirements and procedures for deploying the "
"{productname} MCP Server as a client-managed stdio container or a standalone "
"HTTP service."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-installation.adoc:3
msgid ""
"The MCP Server is available as a container image from the SUSE Container "
"Registry."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-installation.adoc:4
#, no-wrap
msgid "Requirements"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-installation.adoc:5
msgid "Before deployment, ensure that:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-installation.adoc:6
msgid ""
"The deployment environment allows outbound HTTPS connections to the "
"{productname} Server."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-installation.adoc:7
msgid ""
"The {productname} account used by the MCP Server has only the permissions "
"required for the intended tools."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-installation.adoc:8
msgid "A supported MCP client is installed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-installation.adoc:9
msgid ""
"The MCP client supports streamable HTTP and OAuth when these features are "
"required."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-installation.adoc:10
#, no-wrap
msgid "Client-managed container with stdio"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-installation.adoc:11
msgid ""
"In this model, the MCP client starts the container and communicates with it "
"over stdio.  No host port is published."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-installation.adoc:12
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-installation.adoc:21
msgid "Create a protected environment file for the server configuration:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-installation.adoc:13
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"UYUNI_SERVER=https://server.example.com\n"
"UYUNI_USER=mcp-reader\n"
"UYUNI_PASS=replace-me\n"
"UYUNI_MCP_SSL_VERIFY=true\n"
"UYUNI_MCP_WRITE_TOOLS_ENABLED=false\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-installation.adoc:14
msgid ""
"Restrict access to this file because it contains credentials.  See xref:mcp-"
"server-configuration.adoc[Server Configuration] for all settings."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-installation.adoc:15
msgid "Configure the MCP client to run:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-installation.adoc:16
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"podman run -i --rm \\\n"
"  --env-file /absolute/path/to/mcp.env \\\n"
"  registry.suse.com/suse/agentic/mcp/multi-linux-manager:<version>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-installation.adoc:17
msgid ""
"Replace `<version>` with a tested release tag.  Pin a release tag instead of "
"using `latest` in a production configuration."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-installation.adoc:18
msgid ""
"Continue with xref:mcp-server-client-configuration.adoc#client-stdio[stdio "
"client configuration]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-installation.adoc:19
#, no-wrap
msgid "Standalone HTTP server"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-installation.adoc:20
msgid "Use HTTP mode when a persistent service must support multiple clients."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-installation.adoc:22
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"UYUNI_SERVER=https://server.example.com\n"
"UYUNI_MCP_SSL_VERIFY=true\n"
"UYUNI_MCP_WRITE_TOOLS_ENABLED=false\n"
"UYUNI_MCP_TRANSPORT=http\n"
"UYUNI_MCP_HOST=0.0.0.0\n"
"UYUNI_MCP_PORT=8000\n"
"UYUNI_MCP_PUBLIC_URL=https://mcp.example.com\n"
"UYUNI_AUTH_SERVER=https://idp.example.com/realms/mcp\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-installation.adoc:23
msgid ""
"When `UYUNI_AUTH_SERVER` is set, the MCP Server uses each client's OAuth "
"token to authenticate to the {productname} API.  In this configuration, "
"`UYUNI_USER` and `UYUNI_PASS` are not required."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-installation.adoc:24
msgid "Start the container:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-installation.adoc:25
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"podman run --rm \\\n"
"  --env-file /absolute/path/to/mcp.env \\\n"
"  -p 8000:8000 \\\n"
"  registry.suse.com/suse/agentic/mcp/multi-linux-manager:<version>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-installation.adoc:26
msgid ""
"Configure TLS termination for `https://mcp.example.com` and route requests "
"to port `8000`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-installation.adoc:27
msgid "Connect the MCP client to:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-installation.adoc:28
#, no-wrap
msgid "https://mcp.example.com/mcp\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-installation.adoc:29
msgid ""
"The application serves plain HTTP itself.  Do not expose it directly to an "
"untrusted network."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-installation.adoc:30
msgid ""
"If `UYUNI_AUTH_SERVER` is not set, HTTP requests to the MCP Server are "
"unauthenticated.  Only omit authentication for temporary testing on an "
"isolated interface or network."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-installation.adoc:31
msgid ""
"Complete the OAuth configuration described in xref:mcp-server-security."
"adoc#oauth-configuration[OAuth configuration] before allowing user access."
msgstr ""

