#. type: Title =
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-security.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Security"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-security.adoc:2
msgid ""
"This chapter describes authentication, write-tool controls, deployment "
"hardening, and security considerations for AI-assisted operations."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-security.adoc:3
msgid ""
"The MCP Server can query and modify managed infrastructure.  Treat it as a "
"privileged administrative interface."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-security.adoc:4
#, no-wrap
msgid "Security model"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-security.adoc:5
msgid "The server supports two authentication paths:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-security.adoc:6
#, no-wrap
msgid "Basic {productname} authentication"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-security.adoc:7
msgid ""
"In a stdio or trusted deployment, the server logs in with `UYUNI_USER` and "
"`UYUNI_PASS`.  All MCP clients that use that process receive the permissions "
"of this account."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-security.adoc:8
#, no-wrap
msgid "OAuth bearer token"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-security.adoc:9
msgid ""
"In an authenticated HTTP deployment, the MCP Server validates the caller's "
"token and forwards it to the {productname} OIDC login endpoint.  "
"{productname} then maps the token to an existing active user."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-security.adoc:10
msgid ""
"Use a dedicated, least-privileged {productname} account for basic "
"authentication.  For a multi-user HTTP deployment, use OAuth so that actions "
"retain individual user identity and permissions."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-security.adoc:11
#, no-wrap
msgid "OAuth configuration"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-security.adoc:12
msgid ""
"The MCP Server expects an OpenID Connect issuer.  It retrieves signing keys "
"from:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-security.adoc:13
#, no-wrap
msgid "<UYUNI_AUTH_SERVER>/protocol/openid-connect/certs\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-security.adoc:14
msgid "Tokens accepted by the MCP Server must:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-security.adoc:15
msgid "Have an issuer that exactly matches `UYUNI_AUTH_SERVER`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-security.adoc:16
msgid "Include the `mcp-server-uyuni` audience."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-security.adoc:17
msgid "Include the `mcp:read` scope."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-security.adoc:18
msgid "Include the `mcp:write` scope when write tools are enabled."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-security.adoc:19
msgid ""
"Configure the same identity provider on the {productname} Server in `/etc/"
"rhn/rhn.conf`:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-security.adoc:20
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"web.oidc.enabled = true\n"
"web.oidc.idp.issuer = https://idp.example.com/realms/mcp\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-security.adoc:21
msgid "You can explicitly set the JSON Web Key Set path:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-security.adoc:22
#, no-wrap
msgid "web.oidc.idp.jwks_path = /realms/mcp/protocol/openid-connect/certs\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-security.adoc:23
msgid ""
"If the path is not set, {productname} discovers it from the issuer's `/.well-"
"known/openid-configuration` document."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-security.adoc:24
msgid "The default {productname} audience and username claim are:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-security.adoc:25
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"web.oidc.jwt.audience = uyuni-server\n"
"web.oidc.jwt.username_claim = preferred_username\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-security.adoc:26
msgid "The token forwarded to {productname} must include:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-security.adoc:27
msgid ""
"The `uyuni-server` audience, in addition to the `mcp-server-uyuni` audience."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-security.adoc:28
msgid "A `sub` claim."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-security.adoc:29
msgid ""
"A configured username claim whose value matches an existing active "
"{productname} user."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-security.adoc:30
msgid "Restart the relevant {productname} services after changing `rhn.conf`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-security.adoc:31
#, no-wrap
msgid "Write tool controls"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-security.adoc:32
msgid ""
"State-changing tools are not registered unless "
"`UYUNI_MCP_WRITE_TOOLS_ENABLED=true`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-security.adoc:33
msgid ""
"When write tools are enabled, the server asks for confirmation before a "
"change if the MCP client advertises the MCP elicitation capability.  Clients "
"without elicitation support do not receive this server-side confirmation.  "
"Such clients are responsible for their own approval user experience."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-security.adoc:34
msgid ""
"Do not rely on elicitation as the only authorization control.  Use "
"{productname} role-based access control permissions, OAuth scopes, network "
"restrictions, and client-side tool approval policies."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-security.adoc:35
msgid ""
"Enable write tools only for a deployment where they are required.  For high-"
"risk operations:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-security.adoc:36
msgid "Resolve and verify the target system ID."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-security.adoc:37
msgid "Review the generated arguments before approval."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-security.adoc:38
msgid "Apply changes to a small scope first."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-security.adoc:39
msgid "Verify the resulting scheduled action in the {productname} {webui}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-security.adoc:40
msgid ""
"Using the `remove_system` tool is a destructive operation.  When "
"`cleanup=true`, the tool requests forced deletion and cleanup of the system."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-security.adoc:41
#, no-wrap
msgid "Hardening the deployment"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-security.adoc:42
msgid ""
"You can harden the MCP Server deployment by applying the following controls:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-security.adoc:43
msgid "Provide TLS termination for HTTP deployments."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-security.adoc:44
msgid "Never expose unauthenticated HTTP mode to an untrusted network."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-security.adoc:45
msgid "Keep `UYUNI_MCP_SSL_VERIFY=true`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-security.adoc:46
msgid ""
"Store passwords, OAuth configuration, and SSH private keys in a secrets-"
"management system or protected environment file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-security.adoc:47
msgid "Pin the MCP Server container to a reviewed release."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-security.adoc:48
msgid ""
"Use `INFO` or `WARNING` logging in production and protect log files from "
"unauthorized access."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-security.adoc:49
msgid ""
"Restrict network access from the MCP Server to the required {productname} "
"and identity-provider endpoints."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-security.adoc:50
#, no-wrap
msgid "AI and prompt security"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-security.adoc:51
msgid ""
"An AI assistant can use text from prompts and external content when deciding "
"whether and how to call a tool.  This content might contain misleading or "
"malicious instructions.  Treat any tool call based on untrusted content as "
"untrusted until you review it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-security.adoc:52
msgid ""
"Configure the MCP host to require explicit approval for state-changing "
"tools.  Before approval, verify the tool name, target IDs, update or action "
"IDs, and all arguments.  Do not provide secrets in prompts.  Do not ask the "
"model to reproduce environment variables, access tokens, passwords, or "
"private keys."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-tools.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tool Reference"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-tools.adoc:2
msgid ""
"This chapter provides a reference to the tools exposed by the {productname} "
"MCP Server, including their arguments, results, and effects."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-tools.adoc:3
msgid ""
"The {productname} MCP Server exposes read-only tools by default.  Tools in "
"the state-changing section are available only when "
"`UYUNI_MCP_WRITE_TOOLS_ENABLED=true`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-tools.adoc:4
msgid ""
"Most tools that accept `system_identifier` support a system name or system "
"ID.  If a name is not found or is ambiguous, call `find_systems_by_name` and "
"use the returned ID."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-tools.adoc:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "Systems and events"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-tools.adoc:6
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"|Tool\n"
"|Arguments\n"
"|Result\n"
"\n"
"|`list_systems`\n"
"|`limit=50`, `offset=0`\n"
"|Paged active systems. `limit` is capped at 500.\n"
"\n"
"|`get_system_details`\n"
"|`system_identifier`\n"
"|System ID, name, last boot time, UUID, CPU, network, and installed products.\n"
"\n"
"|`get_system_event_history`\n"
"|`system_identifier`, `offset=0`, `limit=10`, optional `earliest_date`\n"
"|Newest-first event history.\n"
"\n"
"|`get_system_event_details`\n"
"|`system_identifier`, `event_id`\n"
"|Status, timestamps, result fields, and additional information for one event.\n"
"\n"
"|`find_systems_by_name`\n"
"|`name`, `limit=50`, `offset=0`\n"
"|Paged hostname matches.\n"
"\n"
"|`find_systems_by_ip`\n"
"|`ip_address`, `limit=50`, `offset=0`\n"
"|Paged systems matching an IP address.\n"
"\n"
"|`list_systems_needing_reboot`\n"
"|`limit=50`, `offset=0`\n"
"|Paged systems requiring a reboot. `limit` is capped at 500.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-tools.adoc:7
#, no-wrap
msgid "Updates and CVEs"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-tools.adoc:8
msgid ""
"The supported advisory type values are `Security Advisory`, `Product "
"Enhancement Advisory`, and `Bug Fix Advisory`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-tools.adoc:9
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"|Tool\n"
"|Arguments\n"
"|Result\n"
"\n"
"|`get_system_updates`\n"
"|`system_identifier`\n"
"|Compact pending update list and counts. CVE expansion is omitted.\n"
"\n"
"|`summarize_system_updates`\n"
"|`system_identifier`, optional `advisory_types`\n"
"|Pending and queued update counts without update details.\n"
"\n"
"|`query_system_updates`\n"
"|`system_identifier`, `limit=25`, `offset=0`, `include_cves=false`, optional `advisory_types`\n"
"|Paged pending updates. A positive `limit` is capped at 200; a non-positive value returns counts without items.\n"
"\n"
"|`check_all_systems_for_updates`\n"
"|`include_updates=false`, `include_cves=false`, `system_limit=25`, `system_offset=0`, `updates_per_system=10`\n"
"|Paged systems with pending updates. `system_limit` is capped at 200.\n"
"\n"
"|`summarize_fleet_updates`\n"
"|`system_limit=25`, `system_offset=0`\n"
"|Paged systems and update counts without update details. `system_limit` is capped at 200.\n"
"\n"
"|`list_systems_needing_update_for_cve`\n"
"|`cve_identifier`, `limit=50`, `offset=0`\n"
"|Paged systems affected by the specified CVE.\n"
"\n"
"|`get_unscheduled_errata`\n"
"|`system_id`\n"
"|Applicable patches that are not scheduled. `system_id` must be a numeric string.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-tools.adoc:10
#, no-wrap
msgid "Actions, activation keys, and groups"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-tools.adoc:11
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"|Tool\n"
"|Arguments\n"
"|Result\n"
"\n"
"|`list_all_scheduled_actions`\n"
"|`limit=50`, `offset=0`, optional `action_types`, optional `scheduler`\n"
"|Paged actions after exact-match filtering. `limit` is capped at 500. The metadata lists observed action types and schedulers for subsequent filters.\n"
"\n"
"|`list_activation_keys`\n"
"|None\n"
"|Activation keys available to the current user.\n"
"\n"
"|`list_system_groups`\n"
"|None\n"
"|Group ID, name, description, and system count.\n"
"\n"
"|`list_group_systems`\n"
"|`group_name`\n"
"|System IDs and names in the specified group.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-tools.adoc:12
#, no-wrap
msgid "State-changing tools"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-tools.adoc:13
msgid ""
"These tools change managed infrastructure.  Review all arguments and the "
"intended targets before approving a call."
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-tools.adoc:14
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"|Tool\n"
"|Arguments\n"
"|Effect\n"
"\n"
"|`schedule_pending_updates_to_system`\n"
"|`system_identifier`\n"
"|Schedules all pending updates for one system.\n"
"\n"
"|`schedule_specific_update`\n"
"|`system_identifier`, `errata_id`\n"
"|Schedules one patch for one system.\n"
"\n"
"|`add_system`\n"
"|`host`, optional `activation_key`, `ssh_port=22`, `ssh_user=root`, `proxy_id`, `salt_ssh=false`\n"
"|Bootstraps and registers a system over SSH. Requires `UYUNI_SSH_PRIV_KEY`. If the client supports elicitation, a missing activation key can be requested interactively.\n"
"\n"
"|`remove_system`\n"
"|`system_identifier`, `cleanup=true`\n"
"|Removes a system. `cleanup=true` requests forced deletion and cleanup; `false` requests no cleanup.\n"
"\n"
"|`schedule_system_reboot`\n"
"|`system_identifier`\n"
"|Schedules an immediate reboot.\n"
"\n"
"|`cancel_action`\n"
"|`action_id`\n"
"|Cancels the specified scheduled action.\n"
"\n"
"|`create_system_group`\n"
"|`name`, optional `description`\n"
"|Creates a system group.\n"
"\n"
"|`add_systems_to_group`\n"
"|`group_name`, `system_identifiers`\n"
"|Adds the specified systems to a group.\n"
"\n"
"|`remove_systems_from_group`\n"
"|`group_name`, `system_identifiers`\n"
"|Removes the specified systems from a group.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-tools.adoc:15
msgid ""
"The `add_system` API can continue processing after the MCP Server request "
"timeout.  When the tool reports that the addition process has started, check "
"the system list later rather than immediately repeating the call."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-tools.adoc:16
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pagination controls"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-tools.adoc:17
msgid ""
"Tools that can return large result sets support pagination with `limit` and "
"`offset` arguments.  Paginated responses include a `meta` object that "
"describes the current page and provides `next_offset` when more results are "
"available.  Pagination limits response size, reduces latency, and lowers AI "
"context usage."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-troubleshooting.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-troubleshooting.adoc:2
msgid ""
"This chapter describes common problems that can occur when configuring or "
"operating the {productname} MCP Server and provides guidance for resolving "
"them."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-troubleshooting.adoc:3
msgid ""
"Start troubleshooting with a read-only tool such as `list_systems`.  Set "
"`UYUNI_MCP_LOG_LEVEL=DEBUG` temporarily when the default log level does not "
"provide enough information.  Debug logs can contain sensitive operational "
"data; protect and remove them according to your logging policy."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-troubleshooting.adoc:4
#, no-wrap
msgid "Startup problems"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-troubleshooting.adoc:5
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"|Message or symptom\n"
"|Resolution\n"
"\n"
"|`Missing required environment variables: UYUNI_SERVER`\n"
"|Set `UYUNI_SERVER` in the environment visible to the MCP Server process. For a client-managed container, verify the absolute path supplied to `--env-file`.\n"
"\n"
"|`UYUNI_SERVER must use http or https and include a host`\n"
"|Use a URL such as `https://server.example.com`.\n"
"\n"
"|`UYUNI_SERVER must not include a path`\n"
"|Remove paths such as `/rhn` and use only the server base URL.\n"
"\n"
"|`UYUNI_MCP_TRANSPORT must be either 'stdio' or 'http'`\n"
"|Set the value to exactly `stdio` or `http`.\n"
"\n"
"|The stdio server disconnects immediately\n"
"|Run the configured command in a terminal and inspect stderr. Verify the image tag, environment-file path, `-i` container option, and {productname} URL.\n"
"\n"
"|The HTTP client receives a connection error\n"
"|Verify the bind address, published port, external route, and that the client URL ends in `/mcp`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-troubleshooting.adoc:6
#, no-wrap
msgid "Authentication and authorization"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-troubleshooting.adoc:7
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"|Message or symptom\n"
"|Resolution\n"
"\n"
"|HTTP 401 or 403 during {productname} login\n"
"|For basic authentication, verify `UYUNI_USER`, `UYUNI_PASS`, account status, and permissions. For OAuth, verify issuer, audiences, scopes, username claim, and the matching active {productname} user.\n"
"\n"
"|OAuth discovery or token validation fails\n"
"|Ensure `UYUNI_MCP_PUBLIC_URL` is the externally reachable HTTPS base URL. Confirm that `UYUNI_AUTH_SERVER` exactly matches the token `iss` claim and that its signing-key endpoint is reachable by the MCP Server.\n"
"\n"
"|MCP authentication succeeds but {productname} OIDC login fails\n"
"|Ensure the token includes both `mcp-server-uyuni` and `uyuni-server` audiences, includes `sub`, and contains the configured username claim.\n"
"\n"
"|A read tool is available but a write tool is missing\n"
"|Set `UYUNI_MCP_WRITE_TOOLS_ENABLED=true` and restart the MCP Server. In OAuth mode, obtain a token with both `mcp:read` and `mcp:write`.\n"
"\n"
"|The user can call a tool but the operation is denied\n"
"|Grant only the required {productname} permissions to the user. MCP availability does not override {productname} authorization.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-troubleshooting.adoc:8
#, no-wrap
msgid "Connectivity and certificates"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-troubleshooting.adoc:9
msgid ""
"A network error or timeout indicates that the MCP Server could not complete "
"a request to {productname}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-troubleshooting.adoc:10
msgid "Resolve `UYUNI_SERVER` from the MCP Server host or container."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-troubleshooting.adoc:11
msgid "Verify TCP and TLS connectivity to the configured port."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-troubleshooting.adoc:12
msgid "Confirm that proxies and firewalls allow the connection."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-troubleshooting.adoc:13
msgid ""
"Verify that the server certificate is valid for the configured hostname and "
"that its CA is trusted."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-troubleshooting.adoc:14
msgid ""
"Increase `UYUNI_MCP_TIMEOUT` only after checking server and network health."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-troubleshooting.adoc:15
msgid "Do not use `UYUNI_MCP_SSL_VERIFY=false` as a permanent certificate fix."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-troubleshooting.adoc:16
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tool-call problems"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/modules/mcp-server/pages/mcp-server-troubleshooting.adoc:17
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"|Message or symptom\n"
"|Resolution\n"
"\n"
"|A system name is not found or resolves ambiguously\n"
"|Call `find_systems_by_name` and pass the numeric `system_id` to the next tool.\n"
"\n"
"|`Invalid system_id ... Provide system_id as a numeric string`\n"
"|The `get_unscheduled_errata` tool does not accept a hostname. Supply the system ID as digits.\n"
"\n"
"|`You need to provide an activation key`\n"
"|The MCP client does not support elicitation. Pass `activation_key` explicitly to `add_system`.\n"
"\n"
"|`UYUNI_SSH_PRIV_KEY environment variable is not set`\n"
"|Set the complete private key with literal `\\n` separators in the MCP Server environment and restart the process.\n"
"\n"
"|System addition reports that the process started\n"
"|The bootstrap request exceeded the request timeout but can still be running on {productname}. Check the system list and server logs before retrying.\n"
"\n"
"|An operation returns `Operation cancelled`\n"
"|The elicitation request was declined, cancelled, or not explicitly approved. Review the arguments and invoke the tool again only if the change is intended.\n"
msgstr ""
